From 17a2718663ad9aa2b94466740f439db37fe8e6e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leviathan <leviathan@vospek.dev>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:35:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] W1-01 ZGC: launch parameter detection and advice

Detects the active GC implementation and scans JVM startup flags for
ZGC-related options. Prints one-time startup advice when ZGC is absent
or heap sizing is suboptimal (-Xms == -Xmx, SoftMaxHeapSize).

The actual JVM flags remain managed by launch scripts; this patch only
observes and advises. Output can be disabled with
-Dleviathan.zgc.advice=false.

Acceptance dimensions tracked here: GC Pause baseline visibility,
Startup advisory cost (none at runtime).
